## Look hardest at
- THE BACKFILL. A store with no ledger must run all migrations exactly as today and then
  record them all. Verify the code does that and NOT any form of detect-which-ran-and-skip,
  which can leave a store half-migrated. This is the single most dangerous thing in the diff.
- Is the ledger write inside the SAME transaction as the migration it records? A migration
  that succeeds while its ledger row is lost re-runs forever; a ledger row written for a
  migration that failed skips it forever. Both are corruption.
- Does 022's runtime column list correctly exclude the four dropped columns and include
  everything else, including columns added by future migrations? What happens on a table
  with an unexpected shape?
- Does the fix hold for a store that legitimately still has the edge columns (an old store
  that never ran 022)?
- Prove the reopen-survival test bites: restore 022 from the parent commit, or disable the
  ledger skip, and confirm TestIssueColumnsSurviveReopen FAILS. Restore every file exactly
  and confirm `git status --porcelain` is clean before you finish.
- claim_test.go is outside the bead's Touches (the manager accepted it: the pre-027 fixture
  relied on migrations re-running, which the ledger makes false). Confirm no assertion was
  weakened to accommodate the fix.

